Rebuild HK-47
Aboard the ../Ebon Hawk/, you'll find a damaged HK unit in the  behind the low security door in the northeast wall of the main hold:

The parts can be acquired from the remains of HK-50 droids encountered, or bought from merchants:

 Part World Area Source Cost HK Vocabulator Peragus II  Administration Level  HK-50 Assassin Droid   HK Control Cluster Telos  Polar Plateau  HK-50   Dantooine  Khoonda Plains    250 HK Droid Processor Dantooine  Khoonda (Plains)  Akkere   HK Chassis Nar Shaddaa  Droid Warehouse  HK-50   Any Nar Shaddaa  Refugee Landing Pad    114-1500 Onderon  Western Square    114-1500

Until HK-47 has been fully repaired, the first part that isn't in your inventory will be added to the inventories of Kodin and 1B-8D when you first speak to them:

 hkpart01 hkpart02 hkpart03 hkpart04 hkpart05 HK Droid Processor HK Chassis HK Control Cluster HK Vocabulator HK Pacifist Package

The most straighforward way to get all four parts is to get the vocabulator on Peragus II and the control cluster on Telos, then go to Nar Shaddaa, where Kodin can sell the droid processor and T3-M4 can get the chassis from the droid warehouse.

However, this means HK-47 cannot be fully repaired and join your party until you escape the destruction of ../Goto's Yacht/, preventing you from using any security console there to upgrade HK-47's combat algorithms (: +1), or gaining ../Influence/ by getting HK-47 to install cryogenic power cells in the refugee quad's . You can fully repair HK-47 beforehand, though, if you have the vocabulator from Peragus II and the control cluster from Telos, buy the droid processor from 1B-8D on Onderon or get it from Akkere's remains on Dantooine, then keep it in your inventory (do not install it in HK-47) until you've spoken to Kodin on Nar Shaddaa to buy the chassis (you could also buy the droid processor from Kodin first, then buy the chassis from 1B-8D).

HK-47 can also be fully repaired before Goto's Yacht if using Restored Content Mod, by exiting the Ebon Hawk on Telos to another HK-50 encounter, where the player may salvage another component from the destroyed HK-50s before buying the final component from Kodin.

If you miss getting a part from a source to which you cannot return, then you can buy it from Kodin or 1B-8D: for example, if you miss the vocabulator on Peragus II then one of them can sell it to you if a droid processor, chassis and control cluster are in your inventory when you first speak to them.

Once you've escaped Peragus II aboard the Ebon Hawk, you can install the vocabulator from the remains of the HK-50 assassin droid encountered in its administration level upon returning from the dormitories:

Once you've left Telos aboard the Ebon Hawk, you can install the control cluster from the remains of one of the HK-50 droids encountered on the polar plateau:

The processor and chassis can both be acquired on Nar Shaddaa, the former from Kodin in the refugee landing pad, and the latter from the remains of one of the HK-50 droids encountered by T3-M4 in the droid warehouse:

